From 9f24d207dffe11ccbfc8d2befd28e6219e6d0bd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Merlin Kooshmanian <mkooshmanian@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Mar 2026 16:42:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] sched/tgbs: add optional root task-group bandwidth
 server

Add an optional TG bandwidth server for the root task group.

When enabled, root-cgroup tasks run on a per-CPU virtual rq served
by a root CBS, while idle and stop tasks remain on the physical rq.

Derive the root runtime from the residual DEADLINE bandwidth left
after its direct children and keep it aligned with the root active
server mask.

Recompute the root reservation when a direct child changes runtime or
period, when a child is onlined or released, when the effective
cpuset changes, or when the global DEADLINE bandwidth is updated.

Account root TG servers in rd->dl_bw.total_bw, including across
runqueue online/offline transitions and root-domain changes.

Disable the physical fair server by default, since FAIR tasks are
served through TG virtual runqueues. Default the global bandwidth
limit to 100% while keeping DEADLINE admission control enabled.
Without child reservations, the root server receives a full period
of runtime without an artificial guard band.

Replenish non-deferred servers immediately when their replenishment
time has already passed, carrying runtime overruns into the next
period. Ignore queued throttle/unthrottle actions that no longer
match the server's state.

With CONFIG_ROOT_TG_BANDWIDTH_SERVER disabled, retain the default
fair-server reservation and the 95% global bandwidth limit.
